    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-16T04:10:57+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-16T04:10:57+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T17:40:57Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-15T17:40:57Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system moving over the southern Tasman Sea extends a ridge over eastern SA until early next week, while a trough lies through the far northwest, before weakening over the weekend. A cold front is forecast to cross the Bight on Monday, extending a trough over western and southern SA.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-16T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-15T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, becoming less likely this morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely north of Marla. Winds east to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h tending north to northeasterly in the morning then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 27 to 32.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:40am to 4:50pm, UV Index predicted to reach 9 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-17T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-18T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-16T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-17T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny morning. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 30s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-18T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-17T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower in the far west in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the afternoon and evening. Winds easterly 15 to 25 km/h turning northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-19T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-20T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-18T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-19T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds north to northeasterly 20 to 30 km/h shifting south to southeasterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 17 and 21 with daytime temperatures reaching 31 to 37.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
